  "comments": "<p>The original entry for this coin listed the decoration on the reverse as a “Kufic calligraphic”. Kufic is the oldest calligraphic form of the various Arabic scripts developed in the 7th century. &nbsp;The design elements are perfectly symmetrical and although somewhat similar in style, there appears to be no calligraphy. &nbsp;Also confirmed in this forum thread: <a href=\"https://en.numista.com/forum/topic167668.html\" rel=\"ugc noopener\" target=\"_blank\" >https://en.numista.com/forum/topic167668.html</a></p>",
